y. 3. **One process binding all three ports** ??? fails the ???kill one HTTP node??? resilience model; rejected. 4. **Docker Compose / containers** ??? prohibited (no DinD / no remote orchestration).  **Trade-off accepted:** `start.sh` must ensure FastAPI/Uvicorn (and `redis` client later) are available via a local venv + pinned `requirements.txt`, preferably with wheels under `vendor/` so boot does not depend on live PyPI. Cold start is slightly heavier than stdlib, but the router seam for sibling tasks is far cleaner.  **Conventions this design locks for the epic (no sibling designs exist yet)** - Product name: **Huddle**; repo root is `/app` at runtime. - HTTP bind: `127.0.0.1` only; ports `8000/8001/8002`. - `node_id` ??? `{0,1,2}` derived solely from port (never from startup order). - API prefix: `/api/...`; JSON only for API responses. - Primary durable store (for later tasks): SQLite file at `/app/data/huddle.db` shared by all nodes via the local filesystem. Redis is **not** the source of truth for users/messages ??? it is for pub/sub fan-out (and optional caches) in later tasks. - Env contract for each node process:   - `HUDDLE_NODE_ID` ??? integer `0|1|2`   - `HUDDLE_PORT` ??? integer `8000|8001|8002`   - `HUDDLE_HOST` ??? `127.0.0.1`   - `HUDDLE_REDIS_URL` ??? `redis://127.0.0.1:6379/0`   - `HUDDLE_DATA_DIR` ??? `/app/data` (or `$APP_ROOT/data`) - Error bodies for unspecified errors: FastAPI default `{\"detail\": ...}` until a later design overrides. - Health **must not** check Redis or SQLite liveness; a live HTTP process alone is enough for `200`.  ## Interface Contracts  ### Process / ops seam (verifier ??? `start.sh`)  | Concern | Contract | |---|---| | Entrypoint | Verifier runs `/app/start.sh` (executable). | | Lifetime | `start.sh` stays in the **foreground** until killed; while it is alive the cluster serves. | | Children | Exactly three HTTP node processes + one `redis-server` (plus any short-lived helpers). | | Ports | HTTP: `127.0.0.1:8000`, `:8